  29:       boundary pixel is diagonally adjacent to the lower half's upper-right boundary pixel.
  30: 
  31:     Key insight:
  32:     - The object is not copied or reflected; it is broken at the horizontal waist,
  33:       recolored by exchanging the two visible object colors, then rejoined diagonally.
